DESCRIPTION:Valentine's Day falls on February 14 and is\, in the United Sta
 tes\, a largely commercial occasion with a genuinely obscure past. The Lib
 rary of Congress calls its origins "murky\," and the honest version of the
  history is a series of plausible connections — a Roman fertility festiv
 al\, one or more martyrs named Valentine\, a Chaucer poem about birds choo
 sing mates — rather than a line of descent anyone can trace end to end.\
